  "description": "<p>The infrastructure to ensure that integration tests are able to run while the port 8080 is in use appears to have been broken in the fcrepo-http-api module.</p>\n\n<p>The following Maven plugin is used to avoid this issue:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/pom.xml#L543-L563\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/pom.xml#L543-L563</a></p>\n\n<p>..in combination with: <br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/pom.xml#L520-L533\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/pom.xml#L520-L533</a></p>\n\n<p>To reproduce:</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>Start tomcat on port 8080</li>\n\t<li>Run 'mvn clean install' on the fcrepo project\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>BOOM! - build fails on fcrepo-http-api integration tests</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>Using \"git bisect\", the following commit appears to have introduced the breakage:<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/commit/90e8f4df99fa43c1bec888154f22245c00ed01d8\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/commit/90e8f4df99fa43c1bec888154f22245c00ed01d8</a></p>\n",
